WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.600
Cardi B threw her shoe
at Nicki Minaj during

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.019
Harper Bazaar's Fashion
Week party, and was swiftly

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:14.764
stopped by Nicki's security.

00:00:15.896 --> 00:00:17.917
So I guess it's safe to assume that there

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:19.947
won't be any collabs in the near future.

00:00:19.947 --> 00:00:21.536
♪ These is bloody shoes ♪ ♪

00:00:21.536 --> 00:00:24.197
Cardi took to Instagram
shortly after the event,

00:00:24.197 --> 00:00:26.725
insinuating that Nicki
had supported negative

00:00:26.725 --> 00:00:29.667
comments about her child
and her parenting styles.

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:33.500
Nicki, fully addressed it
on her Queen radio show,

00:00:41.733 --> 00:00:43.457
Nicki vehemently denied
saying anything negative

00:00:43.457 --> 00:00:45.499
about Cardi's parenting.

00:00:45.499 --> 00:00:48.339
After criticizing Cardi's
attack on her and two

00:00:48.339 --> 00:00:51.219
other women on a separate
occasion, Nicki said

00:00:51.219 --> 00:00:53.537
she found evidence of the
rapper calling another

00:00:53.537 --> 00:00:55.899
woman's black child a monkey.

00:00:55.899 --> 00:00:58.976
The child had passed away,
and Nicki had the mother

00:00:58.976 --> 00:01:01.979
call in to her radio show
to confirm the story.

00:01:01.979 --> 00:01:04.146
The harshest warning came
when Nicki warned Cardi

00:01:04.146 --> 00:01:08.063
about the dangers of her
actions, saying quote...

00:01:11.462 --> 00:01:13.888
While this was definitely
not a direct threat from

00:01:13.888 --> 00:01:17.008
Nicki, it's still really really messy.

00:01:17.008 --> 00:01:20.099
But the Fashion Week
incident is just the latest

00:01:20.099 --> 00:01:22.939
event in a beef that's
been going on for a while.

00:01:22.939 --> 00:01:25.157
Here's how it all began.

00:01:29.597 --> 00:01:31.448
Cardi B entered the
mainstream with her single

00:01:31.448 --> 00:01:34.317
"Bodak Yellow" in June of 2017.

00:01:34.317 --> 00:01:38.149
♪ I don't dance now,
I make money moves ♪ ♪

00:01:38.149 --> 00:01:41.189
Previously, her huge
Instagram presence, mixtapes,

00:01:41.189 --> 00:01:43.979
and scene-stealing appearances
on "Love &amp; Hip-Hop"

00:01:43.979 --> 00:01:46.619
quickly made Cardi an artist to watch.

00:01:46.619 --> 00:01:49.589
"Bodak Yellow" topped the
Billboard charts and she

00:01:49.589 --> 00:01:52.699
became the second female
rapper in history to hold

00:01:52.699 --> 00:01:55.669
the number one spot without any features.

00:01:55.669 --> 00:01:57.752
The first was Lauryn Hill back in 1998.

00:01:58.669 --> 00:02:02.627
And because she's such a
successful female rapper,

00:02:02.627 --> 00:02:06.299
media and fans immediately
began comparing her to

00:02:06.299 --> 00:02:09.557
Nicki, an established and
successful female rapper

00:02:09.557 --> 00:02:12.397
who's been in the game for over a decade.

00:02:12.397 --> 00:02:14.228
♪ Lemme get this straight,
wait, I'm the rookie? ♪ ♪

00:02:14.228 --> 00:02:17.195
At first, the two artists
don't take the bait.

00:02:17.195 --> 00:02:20.099
Nicki actually congratulated
Cardi on Bodak Yellow's

00:02:20.099 --> 00:02:23.488
success, and while Cardi
is shown aligning herself

00:02:23.488 --> 00:02:25.659
with artists that have
notoriously spoke against

00:02:25.659 --> 00:02:29.046
Nicki, like Lil' Kim and
Remy Ma, when asked about

00:02:29.046 --> 00:02:31.717
Nicki, Cardi stays pretty neutral.

00:02:31.717 --> 00:02:34.829
Cardi B: You know, I love
Lil Kim, I love Trina, I

00:02:34.829 --> 00:02:38.746
like Remy Ma, I love
Nicki, I love all of them.

00:02:41.221 --> 00:02:43.304
With the success of her
single, Cardi was asked to

00:02:43.304 --> 00:02:45.936
jump on "MotorSport" with
her now-husband's group,

00:02:45.936 --> 00:02:47.853
Migos, and Nicki Minaj.

00:02:49.026 --> 00:02:51.385
When the song first came
out, rumors spread that

00:02:51.385 --> 00:02:54.307
Nicki didn't know that Cardi
B would be on the track,

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:57.474
and that some lines were direct shots.

00:03:06.816 --> 00:03:08.816
Originally, in the line..

00:03:11.616 --> 00:03:13.454
Quavo was Cardi.

00:03:13.454 --> 00:03:15.288
The whole ordeal resulted
in some genuinely

00:03:15.288 --> 00:03:17.406
hurt feelings, which Nicki revealed on her

00:03:17.406 --> 00:03:19.357
first interview back after a few months'

00:03:19.357 --> 00:03:20.190
hiatus.

00:03:25.429 --> 00:03:28.086
In April 2018, Nicki
gave a raw interview with

00:03:28.086 --> 00:03:30.997
Beats radio, essentially
saying that Cardi didn't

00:03:30.997 --> 00:03:33.008
give her the proper respect
for the "MotorSport"

00:03:33.008 --> 00:03:33.841
feature.

00:03:33.841 --> 00:03:35.397
Cardi B: And when I heard the track

00:03:35.397 --> 00:03:36.230
Host: Right.

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:39.328
Cardi B: Her verse wasn't
finished, or it's not the

00:03:39.328 --> 00:03:42.368
verse that it was now, and you know, Quavo

00:03:42.368 --> 00:03:44.648
told me to get on the
song, and I just felt

00:03:44.648 --> 00:03:48.397
like it was a perfect
opportunity for me to

00:03:48.397 --> 00:03:51.437
be on the track that's big like them.

00:03:51.437 --> 00:03:54.317
Nicki Minaj: The first
interview that she did after

00:03:54.317 --> 00:03:57.117
"MotorSport" came out,
it just really hurt me.

00:03:57.117 --> 00:04:00.826
Cause she looked so aggravated and angry.

00:04:00.826 --> 00:04:02.655
Alana: She said the
incident really hurt her

00:04:02.655 --> 00:04:04.728
feelings, and that she
felt attacked by her

00:04:04.728 --> 00:04:05.645
own people.

00:04:06.755 --> 00:04:09.696
Nicki Minaj: It's because
of the Nicki hate parade

00:04:09.696 --> 00:04:13.216
that she felt the
comfortability to address

00:04:13.216 --> 00:04:14.936
me in that manner.

00:04:19.437 --> 00:04:21.547
Alana: The two spoke at
the Met Gala and it seemed

00:04:21.547 --> 00:04:24.296
their issues were finally put to rest.

00:04:24.296 --> 00:04:26.605
A photographer took a
few shots of the two in a

00:04:26.605 --> 00:04:28.587
seemingly happy conversation.

00:04:28.587 --> 00:04:31.317
According to an interview
with Howard Stern, Cardi

00:04:31.317 --> 00:04:34.208
said that the conversation
was about an issue that

00:04:34.208 --> 00:04:36.541
truly hurt Cardi's feelings.

00:04:39.917 --> 00:04:41.866
Nicki Minaj dropped her
latest album "Queen"

00:04:41.866 --> 00:04:44.317
three months later, and
the internet wasn't done

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:45.717
fanning the flames.

00:04:45.717 --> 00:04:48.637
In a few of her songs,
Nicki takes indirect jabs at

00:04:48.637 --> 00:04:52.887
rappers that fans say may
or may not include Cardi.

00:04:55.683 --> 00:04:57.888
Nicki repeatedly emphasizes
that she writes her own

00:04:57.888 --> 00:05:01.166
bars and that she wants
female rappers to write their

00:05:01.166 --> 00:05:02.859
own bars, too.

00:05:02.859 --> 00:05:05.189
Nicki Minaj: Everybody on the
inside of the industry knows

00:05:05.189 --> 00:05:09.288
that I write my lyrics and
knows that I put so much weight

00:05:09.288 --> 00:05:11.286
on women writing.

00:05:11.286 --> 00:05:13.365
Alana: Cardi B has candidly
said that she doesn't

00:05:13.365 --> 00:05:16.189
write all her own music.
In her recent Queen radio

00:05:16.189 --> 00:05:19.389
episode, Nicki further
takes a jab at Cardi, and

00:05:19.389 --> 00:05:22.349
accuses Cardi of paying
for her tracks to be played

00:05:22.349 --> 00:05:23.432
on the radio.

00:05:33.979 --> 00:05:36.029
ALANA: Before the fame,
it's no secret that Cardi B

00:05:36.029 --> 00:05:37.196
used to strip.

00:05:41.928 --> 00:05:44.117
While Nicki never confirmed
that these lyrics were

00:05:44.117 --> 00:05:47.171
about Cardi B specifically,
it's really hard to deny

00:05:47.171 --> 00:05:50.757
there wasn't the tiniest
bit of shade thrown.

00:05:50.757 --> 00:05:52.699
Nicki Minaj: Oh, no shade.

00:05:52.699 --> 00:05:54.796
Alana: Deep down, I hope
that these two really

00:05:54.796 --> 00:05:57.149
dope artists can just put
their differences aside

00:05:57.149 --> 00:05:59.659
and give their fans the
collabs we all really want.

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:02.269
Do you think that the
tension will die down or are

00:06:02.269 --> 00:06:03.776
they just getting started?

00:06:03.776 --> 00:06:05.977
Let us know in the comments
below and don't forget

00:06:05.977 --> 00:06:07.579
to subscribe!

